import Mettapedia.GSLT.Scope.HolonomyCover
import Mettapedia.TypeTheory.Authority

/-!
# Disparity search: fundamental cycles, a decision procedure and fair enumeration

Views over an index graph glue exactly when holonomy is trivial, and a *disparity* is a closed
walk together with a value of a view that the walk moves (`DisparityAt`).  This module makes the
search for disparities computable and certified.  Read as problem formation: a background process
with no goal forms its problems from disparities, the places where views cannot be integrated as
they stand.  It needs to know where to look (finitely many fundamental cycles), when it may stop
(a decision procedure with certificates on finite systems), and how to look fairly when no
decision is available (a dovetailed, budgeted search that reports only certified disparities and
eventually reports every one).

**Finite generation by fundamental cycles.**  A spanning tree is data, a parent structure with
its proofs (`SpanningTree`): every index other than the root hangs from a parent by one step
(`Step`), and the tree path to an index is the tree path to its parent followed by that step.  The
*fundamental cycle* of an edge runs along the tree to its source, across the edge, and back along
the tree from its target (`SpanningTree.cycle`).
* The fundamental cycle of a tree edge is trivial (`transport_cycle_of_isTreeEdge`), and every walk
  closed through the tree is generated by fundamental cycles, for any equivalence relation on the
  view at the root (`close_related`).
* So holonomy at the root is trivial exactly when every fundamental cycle is
  (`trivialHolonomyAt_iff_cycles`), and, with decidable equality at the root or decidable
  membership in the tree, exactly when the fundamental cycle of every *chord*, an edge outside the
  tree, is (`trivialHolonomyAt_iff_chords`, `trivialHolonomyAt_iff_chords_of_decidable`).  The
  views glue exactly then (`nonempty_gluing_iff_cycles`, `nonempty_gluing_iff_chords`).
* The fundamental cycles generate the register.  Without any decidability, there is no disparity
  at the root exactly when no fundamental cycle moves a value
  (`isEmpty_disparityAt_iff_isEmpty_cycleDisparity`), and none anywhere exactly then
  (`isEmpty_disparity_iff_isEmpty_cycleDisparity`).  With decidable equality at the root, a
  disparity at the root yields, as data, a fundamental cycle that moves a value
  (`cycleDisparityOf`, `nonempty_cycleDisparity_iff`); its edge is a chord
  (`CycleDisparity.not_isTreeEdge`).
* Spanning trees are built without choice for every connected, locally finite index graph whose
  indices have decidable equality.  Rounds of search extend the paths found so far by one step,
  and each index hangs from the parent through which a round first found it (`searchRound`,
  `SpanningTree.ofRounds`; from a listing of the edges, `SpanningTree.ofEdges`).  The root has no
  parent (`SpanningTree.parent_root`).

**A certified decision procedure for finite systems.**  Given a list containing the chords and a
listing of the view at the root (`Listing`) with decidable equality, the search checks fundamental
cycles against values (`SpanningTree.search`); it finds nothing exactly when holonomy at the root
is trivial (`search_eq_none_iff_trivialHolonomyAt`).  Its verdict (`SpanningTree.gluingVerdict`),
an authority outcome, is always decided: it establishes gluing with the gluing built along the
tree, or refutes it with the disparity it found as certificate.  It is correct in both directions
(`gluingVerdict_asBool_eq_true_iff`, `gluingVerdict_asBool_eq_false_iff`,
`not_gluing_of_gluingVerdict_eq_refuted`).  For a finite connected system the tree is built in
rounds from a listing of the edges (`finiteGluingVerdict`), so gluing is decidable
(`decidableNonemptyGluingOfListings`).  For systems given by `Fintype` instances the listings are
merely given, and the answer does not depend on them (`Listing.ofFintype`,
`decidableNonemptyGluingOfFintype`); this version inherits classical choice from membership in the
library's finite sets.

**Fair search without decidable equality.**  When equality of values is not decidable, a finite
search can confirm only a positive form of distinctness: an apartness with a budgeted test that
confirms exactly the apart pairs, at every budget beyond some (`SemiApartness`).  Decidable
equality gives one (`SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq`); boolean streams that differ at some position
give another (`SemiApartness.streams`).
* A schedule examines closed walks and values with budgets.  It is *fair* when every pair is
  examined at some finite stage with at least any given budget (`Fair`).  The dovetailed schedule
  reads each stage through the diagonal enumeration of pairs twice, as a pair of ranks and a
  budget (`diagonal`, `exists_diagonal_eq`, `dovetail`).  It examines every listed pair at every
  budget at a finite stage (`dovetail_examines`), so it is fair when the walks and values are
  enumerated (`dovetail_fair`).  On a locally finite index graph the closed walks at the root are
  enumerated, read from lists of ranks of the steps out of each index (`walkOfRanks`,
  `listOfRank`, `closedWalkOfRank`, `exists_closedWalkOfRank_eq`), so the dovetailed search over
  all closed walks is fair as soon as the view at the root is enumerated
  (`dovetail_closedWalks_fair`).
* Nothing is reported without a certificate: a report is a closed walk with a value it moves
  apart, confirmed at the budget of its stage (`ApartDisparity`, `examine_sound`).  A fair
  schedule reports every disparity witnessed by apartness at some finite stage
  (`examine_complete`, `examine_dovetail`), so the register is semi-decidable
  (`exists_examine_iff`).  When distinctness implies apartness, every disparity is reported
  (`examine_complete_of_tight`).
* Fundamental cycles suffice without decidable equality when the apartness is symmetric and
  cotransitive (`SemiApartness.Cotransitive`, which holds for decidable equality and for
  streams): if a closed walk moves a value apart, some fundamental cycle moves some value apart
  (`exists_cycle_apart_of_close`, `exists_cycle_apart`).  So the dovetailed search over the
  fundamental cycles of enumerated edges and the enumerated values reports a disparity whenever
  one exists (`exists_examine_cycles`).
* The budgeted verdict on gluing (`searchVerdict`) only refines as the budget grows
  (`searchVerdict_budget_mono`): it is incomplete until a disparity is confirmed and then refutes
  gluing with it as certificate (`not_gluing_of_searchVerdict_eq_refuted`,
  `exists_searchVerdict_refuted`).  A finite search never establishes gluing
  (`searchVerdict_ne_established`).

**Controls.**
* The twisted three-cycle.  With `b` hanging from `a` and `c` from `b`, the only chord is `ca`
  (`Twisted.tree_chordList`).  Its fundamental cycle is the twist (`Twisted.tree_cycle_ca`), while
  that of the tree edge `ab` is trivial (`Twisted.tree_cycle_ab`).  The search finds the disparity
  at this one fundamental cycle (`Twisted.tree_search`), and the verdict refutes gluing with it
  (`Twisted.tree_gluingVerdict`).  The tree built in rounds hangs `c` from `a` instead, with the
  chord `bc` (`Twisted.roundsTree_chordList`), and the finite procedure refutes gluing
  (`Twisted.finiteGluingVerdict_refutes`) with the disparity at that chord
  (`Twisted.finiteGluingVerdict_eq`).
* The untwisted path has no chord (`Twisted.pathTree_chordList`), and the verdict establishes
  gluing (`Twisted.pathTree_gluingVerdict`).
* The swapped three-cycle: the search passes over the fixed point `0` and finds `1`
  (`Swap.tree_search`).  The fair search over all closed walks and all points reports every
  disparity of the swapped cycle (`Swap.closedWalks_search_complete`,
  `Swap.closedWalks_search_reports`), and so does the search over its three fundamental cycles
  (`Swap.cycles_search_reports`).
* A spanning tree is needed.  Two indices without edges have trivial holonomy at the root but no
  gluing, and no spanning tree (`Apart.trivial_at_root_without_tree`).  A parent assignment around
  the twisted cycle makes every edge a parent link, so no chord would remain to check, yet the
  cycle has a disparity; no spanning tree uses that assignment, since a root has no parent
  (`Twisted.cyclic_parents_not_tree`).
* Dovetailing is needed.  Examining every closed walk of the swapped cycle with only the fixed
  point never reports and is not fair (`Swap.firstValueOnly_misses`,
  `Swap.firstValueOnly_not_fair`), while the dovetailed search finds the disparity
  (`Swap.dovetail_finds`).  On a loop that flips position `1` of boolean streams, a fixed budget
  `0` never reports and is not fair (`FlipStream.zeroBudget_misses`,
  `FlipStream.zeroBudget_not_fair`).  The test confirms the disparity at budget `1` and not at
  budget `0` (`FlipStream.turn_test`); the dovetailed search finds it (`FlipStream.dovetail_finds`),
  and its verdict is incomplete after two stages and refutes gluing after three
  (`FlipStream.searchVerdict_stages`).  Three turns around the loop reduce to its fundamental
  cycle without decidable equality of streams (`FlipStream.thrice_reduces`).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace Mettapedia.GSLT.Scope

open Mettapedia.TypeTheory.AuthorityTheory (Outcome)

universe uI uE uV u v

/-! ## Listings and the diagonal enumeration -/

namespace DisparitySearch

/-- **A finite listing** of a type: a list in which every element occurs. -/
structure Listing (α : Type u) where
  /-- The listed elements. -/
  elems : List α
  /-- Every element is listed. -/
  complete : ∀ a : α, a ∈ elems

/-- A `Fintype` instance merely provides a listing.  Membership in the library's finite sets
depends on classical choice, so this bridge does too. -/
def Listing.ofFintype (α : Type u) [Fintype α] : Trunc (Listing α) :=
  Quotient.recOnSubsingleton
    (motive := fun s : Multiset α => (∀ a : α, a ∈ s) → Trunc (Listing α))
    (Finset.univ : Finset α).val
    (fun elems complete => Trunc.mk ⟨elems, fun a => Multiset.mem_coe.mp (complete a)⟩)
    fun a => Finset.mem_def.mp (Finset.mem_univ a)

/-- One step of the diagonal walk through pairs of ranks. -/
def diagonalStep : ℕ × ℕ → ℕ × ℕ
  | (0, second) => (second + 1, 0)
  | (first + 1, second) => (first, second + 1)

/-- **The diagonal enumeration of pairs**: `(0, 0), (1, 0), (0, 1), (2, 0), (1, 1), (0, 2), …`,
each diagonal walked from the first axis to the second. -/
def diagonal : ℕ → ℕ × ℕ
  | 0 => (0, 0)
  | stage + 1 => diagonalStep (diagonal stage)

/-- Along a diagonal, `k` stages move `k` from the first rank to the second. -/
theorem diagonal_walk (stage : ℕ) :
    ∀ (k first second : ℕ), diagonal stage = (first + k, second) →
      diagonal (stage + k) = (first, second + k)
  | 0, _, _, at_ => at_
  | k + 1, first, second, at_ => by
    have walked := diagonal_walk stage k (first + 1) second
      (at_.trans (Prod.ext (by omega) rfl))
    show diagonalStep (diagonal (stage + k)) = (first, second + (k + 1))
    rw [walked]
    rfl

theorem exists_diagonal_eq_first : ∀ first : ℕ, ∃ stage, diagonal stage = (first, 0)
  | 0 => ⟨0, rfl⟩
  | first + 1 => by
    obtain ⟨stage, at_⟩ := exists_diagonal_eq_first first
    have walked := diagonal_walk stage first 0 0
      (at_.trans (Prod.ext (Nat.zero_add first).symm rfl))
    refine ⟨stage + first + 1, ?_⟩
    show diagonalStep (diagonal (stage + first)) = (first + 1, 0)
    rw [walked, Nat.zero_add]
    rfl

/-- **Every pair of ranks occurs** in the diagonal enumeration. -/
theorem exists_diagonal_eq (first second : ℕ) : ∃ stage, diagonal stage = (first, second) := by
  obtain ⟨stage, at_⟩ := exists_diagonal_eq_first (first + second)
  exact ⟨stage + second, (diagonal_walk stage second first 0 at_).trans
    (Prod.ext rfl (Nat.zero_add second))⟩

/-- Along the diagonal enumeration, the two ranks never exceed the stage. -/
theorem diagonal_sum_le : ∀ stage : ℕ, (diagonal stage).1 + (diagonal stage).2 ≤ stage
  | 0 => Nat.le_refl 0
  | stage + 1 => by
    have previous := diagonal_sum_le stage
    show (diagonalStep (diagonal stage)).1 + (diagonalStep (diagonal stage)).2 ≤ stage + 1
    cases at_ : diagonal stage with
    | mk first second =>
      rw [at_] at previous
      cases first with
      | zero =>
        show second + 1 + 0 ≤ stage + 1
        omega
      | succ first =>
        show first + (second + 1) ≤ stage + 1
        omega

/-- **The lists of ranks, enumerated**: rank `0` is the empty list, and rank `n + 1` reads `n`
through the diagonal enumeration as the head and the rank of the tail. -/
def listOfRank : ℕ → List ℕ
  | 0 => []
  | stage + 1 => (diagonal stage).1 :: listOfRank (diagonal stage).2
termination_by stage => stage
decreasing_by
  have := diagonal_sum_le stage
  omega

/-- **Every list of ranks occurs** at some rank. -/
theorem exists_listOfRank_eq : ∀ ranks : List ℕ, ∃ stage, listOfRank stage = ranks
  | [] => ⟨0, by rw [listOfRank]⟩
  | rank :: ranks => by
    obtain ⟨tail, tailAt⟩ := exists_listOfRank_eq ranks
    obtain ⟨stage, pairAt⟩ := exists_diagonal_eq rank tail
    refine ⟨stage + 1, ?_⟩
    rw [listOfRank, pairAt, tailAt]

/-- **The dovetailed schedule** of two sequences.  Stage `n` reads the diagonal pair
`(k, budget)`, reads `k` again as a pair of ranks `(r, s)`, and examines the `r`-th item of the
first sequence with the `s`-th item of the second at that budget. -/
def dovetail {α : Type u} {β : Type v} (first : ℕ → Option α) (second : ℕ → Option β)
    (stage : ℕ) : Option ((α × β) × ℕ) :=
  match first (diagonal (diagonal stage).1).1, second (diagonal (diagonal stage).1).2 with
  | some a, some b => some ((a, b), (diagonal stage).2)
  | _, _ => none

/-- **Dovetailing examines every listed pair at every budget**, each at a finite stage. -/
theorem dovetail_examines {α : Type u} {β : Type v} {first : ℕ → Option α}
    {second : ℕ → Option β} {a : α} {b : β} {r s : ℕ} (listedFirst : first r = some a)
    (listedSecond : second s = some b) (budget : ℕ) :
    ∃ stage, dovetail first second stage = some ((a, b), budget) := by
  obtain ⟨k, pairAt⟩ := exists_diagonal_eq r s
  obtain ⟨stage, stageAt⟩ := exists_diagonal_eq k budget
  refine ⟨stage, ?_⟩
  have rankAt : (diagonal stage).1 = k := by rw [stageAt]
  have budgetAt : (diagonal stage).2 = budget := by rw [stageAt]
  have firstAt : (diagonal (diagonal stage).1).1 = r := by rw [rankAt, pairAt]
  have secondAt : (diagonal (diagonal stage).1).2 = s := by rw [rankAt, pairAt]
  unfold dovetail
  rw [firstAt, secondAt, listedFirst, listedSecond, budgetAt]

/-- A schedule of examinations, each an item with a budget, is **fair** when every item is
examined at some finite stage with at least any given budget. -/
def Fair {Item : Type u} (schedule : ℕ → Option (Item × ℕ)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (item : Item) (budget : ℕ),
    ∃ stage budget', budget ≤ budget' ∧ schedule stage = some (item, budget')

/-- **Dovetailing is fair** when both sequences list every item. -/
theorem dovetail_fair {α : Type u} {β : Type v} {first : ℕ → Option α}
    {second : ℕ → Option β} (listsFirst : ∀ a : α, ∃ r, first r = some a)
    (listsSecond : ∀ b : β, ∃ s, second s = some b) :
    Fair (dovetail first second) := by
  rintro ⟨a, b⟩ budget
  obtain ⟨r, listedFirst⟩ := listsFirst a
  obtain ⟨s, listedSecond⟩ := listsSecond b
  obtain ⟨stage, examined⟩ := dovetail_examines listedFirst listedSecond budget
  exact ⟨stage, budget, Nat.le_refl budget, examined⟩

/-- **A semi-decidable apartness**: a relation that implies distinctness, with a budgeted test.
The test confirms only apart pairs, confirms every apart pair at some budget, and keeps
confirming at larger budgets. -/
structure SemiApartness (α : Type u) where
  /-- The positive form of distinctness that a finite search can confirm. -/
  Apart : α → α → Prop
  ne_of_apart : ∀ {a b : α}, Apart a b → a ≠ b
  /-- The budgeted test. -/
  test : α → α → ℕ → Bool
  test_sound : ∀ {a b : α} {budget : ℕ}, test a b budget = true → Apart a b
  test_complete : ∀ {a b : α}, Apart a b → ∃ budget, test a b budget = true
  test_mono : ∀ {a b : α} {small large : ℕ}, small ≤ large → test a b small = true →
    test a b large = true

/-- **Decidable equality is a semi-decidable apartness**, decided at every budget. -/
def SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq (α : Type u) [DecidableEq α] : SemiApartness α where
  Apart a b := a ≠ b
  ne_of_apart apart := apart
  test a b _ := decide (a ≠ b)
  test_sound confirmed := of_decide_eq_true confirmed
  test_complete apart := ⟨0, decide_eq_true apart⟩
  test_mono _ confirmed := confirmed

/-- **Boolean streams are apart** when they differ at some position; the test with budget `n`
compares the positions up to `n`.  Equality of streams is not decidable, and distinctness
implies apartness only by a classical step. -/
def SemiApartness.streams : SemiApartness (ℕ → Bool) where
  Apart f g := ∃ k, f k ≠ g k
  ne_of_apart := fun ⟨k, differ⟩ same => differ (congrFun same k)
  test f g budget := (List.range (budget + 1)).any fun k => f k != g k
  test_sound confirmed := by
    obtain ⟨k, _, differ⟩ := List.any_eq_true.mp confirmed
    exact ⟨k, bne_iff_ne.mp differ⟩
  test_complete := fun ⟨k, differ⟩ =>
    ⟨k, List.any_eq_true.mpr
      ⟨k, List.mem_range.mpr (Nat.lt_succ_self k), bne_iff_ne.mpr differ⟩⟩
  test_mono le confirmed := by
    obtain ⟨k, below, differ⟩ := List.any_eq_true.mp confirmed
    exact List.any_eq_true.mpr
      ⟨k, List.mem_range.mpr (by have := List.mem_range.mp below; omega), differ⟩

/-- An apartness is **symmetric and cotransitive** when apart points are apart in either order,
and any third point is apart from one of them. -/
structure SemiApartness.Cotransitive {α : Type u} (apartness : SemiApartness α) : Prop where
  symm : ∀ {a b : α}, apartness.Apart a b → apartness.Apart b a
  cotrans : ∀ {a b : α} (c : α), apartness.Apart a b →
    apartness.Apart a c ∨ apartness.Apart c b

theorem SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq_cotransitive (α : Type u) [DecidableEq α] :
    (SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq α).Cotransitive where
  symm different same := different same.symm
  cotrans := fun {a _} c different =>
    if same : a = c then .inr fun same' => different (same.trans same') else .inl same

theorem SemiApartness.streams_cotransitive : SemiApartness.streams.Cotransitive where
  symm := fun ⟨k, differ⟩ => ⟨k, fun same => differ same.symm⟩
  cotrans := fun c ⟨k, differ⟩ =>
    if same : _ = c k then .inr ⟨k, fun same' => differ (same.trans same')⟩
    else .inl ⟨k, same⟩

end DisparitySearch

namespace ViewSystem

open DisparitySearch

variable {Index : Type uI} {S : ViewSystem.{uI, uE, uV} Index}

/-! ## Steps and spanning trees -/

variable (S) in
/-- **One step**: an edge of the index graph crossed from `i` to `j`, forward or backward. -/
inductive Step (i j : Index) : Type uE
  | forward (edge : S.Edge i j)
  | backward (edge : S.Edge j i)

/-- A step as a walk of length one. -/
def Step.toWalk {i j : Index} : S.Step i j → S.Walk i j
  | .forward edge => .forward edge (.nil j)
  | .backward edge => .backward edge (.nil j)

instance [∀ i j : Index, DecidableEq (S.Edge i j)] {i j : Index} : DecidableEq (S.Step i j)
  | .forward first, .forward second =>
    if same : first = second then isTrue (congrArg Step.forward same)
    else isFalse fun equal => same (Step.forward.inj equal)
  | .backward first, .backward second =>
    if same : first = second then isTrue (congrArg Step.backward same)
    else isFalse fun equal => same (Step.backward.inj equal)
  | .forward _, .backward _ => isFalse fun equal => nomatch equal
  | .backward _, .forward _ => isFalse fun equal => nomatch equal

/-- The number of edges a walk crosses. -/
def Walk.length : {i j : Index} → S.Walk i j → ℕ
  | _, _, .nil _ => 0
  | _, _, .forward _ rest => rest.length + 1
  | _, _, .backward _ rest => rest.length + 1

/-- A walk followed by one step is never empty. -/
theorem Walk.append_toWalk_ne_nil {i j : Index} (walk : S.Walk i j) (step : S.Step j i) :
    walk.append step.toWalk ≠ .nil i := by
  cases walk with
  | nil => cases step <;> exact fun equal => nomatch equal
  | forward edge rest => exact fun equal => nomatch equal
  | backward edge rest => exact fun equal => nomatch equal

variable (S) in
/-- **A spanning tree** rooted at `root`, as a parent structure with its proofs: every index other
than the root has a parent link, one step from its parent, and the tree path from the root to an
index is the tree path to its parent followed by that step. -/
structure SpanningTree (root : Index) where
  /-- The parent link: the parent and the step from it. -/
  parent : ∀ j : Index, Option (Σ p : Index, S.Step p j)
  /-- The tree path from the root. -/
  path : ∀ j : Index, S.Walk root j
  path_root : path root = .nil root
  /-- Only the root lacks a parent. -/
  eq_root : ∀ j : Index, parent j = none → j = root
  path_parent : ∀ (j p : Index) (step : S.Step p j), parent j = some ⟨p, step⟩ →
    path j = (path p).append step.toWalk

namespace SpanningTree

variable {root : Index} (T : S.SpanningTree root)

/-- The root has no parent. -/
theorem parent_root : T.parent root = none := by
  cases linked : T.parent root with
  | none => rfl
  | some link =>
    exact absurd ((T.path_parent root link.1 link.2 linked).symm.trans T.path_root)
      (Walk.append_toWalk_ne_nil _ _)

/-- The connectivity a spanning tree witnesses. -/
def connect (j : Index) : Trunc (S.Walk root j) :=
  Trunc.mk (T.path j)

/-- **The fundamental cycle** of an edge: along the tree to its source, across the edge, and back
along the tree from its target. -/
def cycle {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j) : S.Walk root root :=
  (T.path i).append (.forward edge (T.path j).reverse)

theorem transport_cycle {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j) (value : S.View root) :
    S.transport (T.cycle edge) value =
      S.transport (T.path j).reverse (S.translate edge (S.transport (T.path i) value)) :=
  transport_append _ _ value

/-- An edge **belongs to the tree** when it is the parent link of its target, crossed forward, or
of its source, crossed backward.  The other edges are the chords. -/
def IsTreeEdge {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j) : Prop :=
  T.parent j = some ⟨i, .forward edge⟩ ∨ T.parent i = some ⟨j, .backward edge⟩

instance [DecidableEq Index] [∀ i j : Index, DecidableEq (S.Edge i j)] {i j : Index}
    (edge : S.Edge i j) : Decidable (T.IsTreeEdge edge) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (_ ∨ _))

/-- **The fundamental cycle of a tree edge is trivial**: it goes out along the tree and comes
back the same way. -/
theorem transport_cycle_of_isTreeEdge {i j : Index} {edge : S.Edge i j}
    (tree : T.IsTreeEdge edge) (value : S.View root) :
    S.transport (T.cycle edge) value = value := by
  rw [transport_cycle]
  rcases tree with down | up
  · have forth : S.transport (T.path j) value =
        S.translate edge (S.transport (T.path i) value) := by
      rw [T.path_parent j i (.forward edge) down, transport_append]
      rfl
    rw [← forth, transport_reverse]
  · have back : S.transport (T.path i) value =
        (S.translate edge).symm (S.transport (T.path j) value) := by
      rw [T.path_parent i j (.backward edge) up, transport_append]
      rfl
    rw [back, Equiv.apply_symm_apply, transport_reverse]

/-! ## Finite generation by fundamental cycles -/

/-- **Close a walk through the tree**: along the tree to its start, along the walk, and back along
the tree from its end. -/
def close {i j : Index} (walk : S.Walk i j) : S.Walk root root :=
  (T.path i).append (walk.append (T.path j).reverse)

theorem transport_close_nil (i : Index) (value : S.View root) :
    S.transport (T.close (.nil i)) value = value := by
  change S.transport ((T.path i).append (T.path i).reverse) value = value
  rw [transport_append, transport_reverse]

theorem transport_close_forward {i k j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i k) (rest : S.Walk k j)
    (value : S.View root) :
    S.transport (T.close (.forward edge rest)) value =
      S.transport (T.close rest) (S.transport (T.cycle edge) value) := by
  change S.transport ((T.path i).append (.forward edge (rest.append (T.path j).reverse))) value =
    S.transport ((T.path k).append (rest.append (T.path j).reverse))
      (S.transport (T.cycle edge) value)
  rw [transport_append, transport_append, transport_cycle, transport_reverse_right]
  rfl

/-- Back along the fundamental cycle of an edge `k → i`, then along the tree to `k`: the same as
along the tree to `i`, then back across the edge. -/
theorem transport_path_cycle_reverse {i k : Index} (edge : S.Edge k i) (value : S.View root) :
    S.transport (T.path k) (S.transport (T.cycle edge).reverse value) =
      (S.translate edge).symm (S.transport (T.path i) value) := by
  have round := transport_reverse_right (T.cycle edge) value
  rw [transport_cycle] at round
  have forth := congrArg (S.transport (T.path i)) round
  rw [transport_reverse_right] at forth
  rw [← forth, Equiv.symm_apply_apply]

theorem transport_close_backward {i k j : Index} (edge : S.Edge k i) (rest : S.Walk k j)
    (value : S.View root) :
    S.transport (T.close (.backward edge rest)) value =
      S.transport (T.close rest) (S.transport (T.cycle edge).reverse value) := by
  change S.transport ((T.path i).append (.backward edge (rest.append (T.path j).reverse))) value =
    S.transport ((T.path k).append (rest.append (T.path j).reverse))
      (S.transport (T.cycle edge).reverse value)
  rw [transport_append, transport_append, transport_path_cycle_reverse]
  rfl

/-- A closed walk at the root, closed through the tree, transports as the walk itself. -/
theorem transport_close_root (loop : S.Walk root root) (value : S.View root) :
    S.transport (T.close loop) value = S.transport loop value := by
  change S.transport ((T.path root).append (loop.append (T.path root).reverse)) value = _
  rw [T.path_root]
  change S.transport (loop.append (.nil root)) value = _
  rw [transport_append]
  rfl

/-- **Fundamental cycles generate**: for any equivalence relation on the view at the root that
relates the transport of every value along every fundamental cycle to the value, the transport of
every value along every walk closed through the tree is related to the value. -/
theorem close_related (rel : S.View root → S.View root → Prop) (equivalence : Equivalence rel)
    (cycles : ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j) (value : S.View root),
      rel (S.transport (T.cycle edge) value) value)
    {i j : Index} (walk : S.Walk i j) (value : S.View root) :
    rel (S.transport (T.close walk) value) value := by
  induction walk generalizing value with
  | nil i =>
    rw [T.transport_close_nil]
    exact equivalence.refl _
  | forward edge rest ih =>
    rw [T.transport_close_forward]
    exact equivalence.trans (ih _) (cycles edge value)
  | backward edge rest ih =>
    rw [T.transport_close_backward]
    refine equivalence.trans (ih _) (equivalence.symm ?_)
    have back := cycles edge (S.transport (T.cycle edge).reverse value)
    rwa [transport_reverse_right] at back

/-- **Finite generation**: holonomy at the root is trivial exactly when the fundamental cycle of
every edge transports every value to itself. -/
theorem trivialHolonomyAt_iff_cycles :
    S.TrivialHolonomyAt root ↔
      ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j) (value : S.View root),
        S.transport (T.cycle edge) value = value := by
  constructor
  · intro trivial i j edge value
    exact trivial (T.cycle edge) value
  · intro cycles loop value
    rw [← T.transport_close_root]
    exact T.close_related Eq eq_equivalence cycles loop value

/-- **Finite generation by the chords**, for views with decidable equality at the root: holonomy
at the root is trivial exactly when the fundamental cycle of every chord, an edge outside the
tree, transports every value to itself. -/
theorem trivialHolonomyAt_iff_chords [DecidableEq (S.View root)] :
    S.TrivialHolonomyAt root ↔
      ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j), ¬ T.IsTreeEdge edge →
        ∀ value : S.View root, S.transport (T.cycle edge) value = value := by
  rw [T.trivialHolonomyAt_iff_cycles]
  constructor
  · intro cycles i j edge _ value
    exact cycles edge value
  · intro chords i j edge value
    exact if fixed : S.transport (T.cycle edge) value = value then fixed
      else absurd (chords edge (fun tree => fixed (T.transport_cycle_of_isTreeEdge tree value))
        value) fixed

/-- **Finite generation by the chords**, for decidable membership in the tree; no decidable
equality of values is needed. -/
theorem trivialHolonomyAt_iff_chords_of_decidable
    (decideTree : ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j), Decidable (T.IsTreeEdge edge)) :
    S.TrivialHolonomyAt root ↔
      ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j), ¬ T.IsTreeEdge edge →
        ∀ value : S.View root, S.transport (T.cycle edge) value = value := by
  rw [T.trivialHolonomyAt_iff_cycles]
  constructor
  · intro cycles i j edge _ value
    exact cycles edge value
  · intro chords i j edge value
    exact match decideTree edge with
      | isTrue tree => T.transport_cycle_of_isTreeEdge tree value
      | isFalse chord => chords edge chord value

/-- **The views glue exactly when every fundamental cycle is trivial.** -/
theorem nonempty_gluing_iff_cycles :
    Nonempty S.Gluing ↔
      ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j) (value : S.View root),
        S.transport (T.cycle edge) value = value :=
  (nonempty_gluing_iff T.connect).trans
    ((trivialHolonomy_iff_at T.connect).trans T.trivialHolonomyAt_iff_cycles)

/-- **The views glue exactly when the fundamental cycle of every chord is trivial**, for views
with decidable equality at the root. -/
theorem nonempty_gluing_iff_chords [DecidableEq (S.View root)] :
    Nonempty S.Gluing ↔
      ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j), ¬ T.IsTreeEdge edge →
        ∀ value : S.View root, S.transport (T.cycle edge) value = value :=
  (nonempty_gluing_iff T.connect).trans
    ((trivialHolonomy_iff_at T.connect).trans T.trivialHolonomyAt_iff_chords)

/-! ## Disparities at fundamental cycles -/

/-- **A disparity at a fundamental cycle**: an edge whose fundamental cycle moves a value of the
view at the root. -/
structure CycleDisparity where
  /-- The source of the edge. -/
  source : Index
  /-- The target of the edge. -/
  target : Index
  /-- The edge. -/
  edge : S.Edge source target
  /-- The value its fundamental cycle moves. -/
  value : S.View root
  moved : S.transport (T.cycle edge) value ≠ value

variable {T} in
/-- A disparity at a fundamental cycle is a disparity at the root. -/
def CycleDisparity.toDisparityAt (disparity : T.CycleDisparity) : S.DisparityAt root :=
  ⟨T.cycle disparity.edge, disparity.value, disparity.moved⟩

variable {T} in
/-- The edge of a disparity at a fundamental cycle is a chord. -/
theorem CycleDisparity.not_isTreeEdge (disparity : T.CycleDisparity) :
    ¬ T.IsTreeEdge disparity.edge :=
  fun tree => disparity.moved (T.transport_cycle_of_isTreeEdge tree disparity.value)

/-- **The fundamental cycles generate the register at the root**, without any decidability: there
is no disparity at the root exactly when no fundamental cycle moves a value. -/
theorem isEmpty_disparityAt_iff_isEmpty_cycleDisparity :
    IsEmpty (S.DisparityAt root) ↔ IsEmpty T.CycleDisparity := by
  constructor
  · intro empty
    exact ⟨fun disparity => empty.false disparity.toDisparityAt⟩
  · intro empty
    rw [isEmpty_disparityAt_iff_not_not]
    intro loop value
    have stable := T.close_related (fun first second => ¬¬ first = second)
      ⟨fun _ absurdity => absurdity rfl,
        fun related absurdity => related fun same => absurdity same.symm,
        fun first second absurdity =>
          first fun same => second fun same' => absurdity (same.trans same')⟩
      (fun edge value moved => empty.false ⟨_, _, edge, value, moved⟩) loop value
    rwa [T.transport_close_root] at stable

/-- **The fundamental cycles generate the whole register**: on the index graph a spanning tree
connects, there is no disparity anywhere exactly when no fundamental cycle moves a value. -/
theorem isEmpty_disparity_iff_isEmpty_cycleDisparity :
    IsEmpty S.Disparity ↔ IsEmpty T.CycleDisparity :=
  Iff.trans
    ⟨fun empty => ⟨fun disparity => empty.false ⟨root, disparity⟩⟩,
      fun empty => ⟨fun disparity => Trunc.induction_on (β := fun _ => False)
        (disparity.toRoot T.connect) fun found => empty.false found⟩⟩
    T.isEmpty_disparityAt_iff_isEmpty_cycleDisparity

/-- **Find the fundamental cycle that moves**: with decidable equality at the root, a walk closed
through the tree that moves a value yields a fundamental cycle that moves a value. -/
def findCycleDisparity [DecidableEq (S.View root)] :
    {i j : Index} → (walk : S.Walk i j) → (value : S.View root) →
      S.transport (T.close walk) value ≠ value → T.CycleDisparity
  | _, _, .nil i, value, moved => absurd (T.transport_close_nil i value) moved
  | _, _, .forward edge rest, value, moved =>
    if fixed : S.transport (T.cycle edge) value = value then
      findCycleDisparity rest value fun same => moved
        ((T.transport_close_forward edge rest value).trans
          ((congrArg (S.transport (T.close rest)) fixed).trans same))
    else ⟨_, _, edge, value, fixed⟩
  | _, _, .backward edge rest, value, moved =>
    if fixed : S.transport (T.cycle edge).reverse value = value then
      findCycleDisparity rest value fun same => moved
        ((T.transport_close_backward edge rest value).trans
          ((congrArg (S.transport (T.close rest)) fixed).trans same))
    else ⟨_, _, edge, S.transport (T.cycle edge).reverse value, fun same =>
      fixed ((transport_reverse_right (T.cycle edge) value).symm.trans same).symm⟩

/-- **Every disparity at the root yields a disparity at a fundamental cycle**, for decidable
equality at the root. -/
def cycleDisparityOf [DecidableEq (S.View root)] (disparity : S.DisparityAt root) :
    T.CycleDisparity :=
  T.findCycleDisparity disparity.loop disparity.value fun same =>
    disparity.moved ((T.transport_close_root disparity.loop disparity.value).symm.trans same)

/-- **If any disparity exists, one exists at a fundamental cycle**, for decidable equality at the
root. -/
theorem nonempty_cycleDisparity_iff [DecidableEq (S.View root)] :
    Nonempty T.CycleDisparity ↔ Nonempty (S.DisparityAt root) :=
  ⟨fun ⟨disparity⟩ => ⟨disparity.toDisparityAt⟩,
    fun ⟨disparity⟩ => ⟨T.cycleDisparityOf disparity⟩⟩

end SpanningTree

/-! ## Building a spanning tree in rounds -/

section Rounds

variable [DecidableEq Index]

/-- **Round `n` of the search for a spanning tree** of a locally finite index graph, given the
steps into every index.  Round `0` finds the root, with no parent and the empty path; round
`n + 1` keeps what round `n` found and finds every other index through the first listed step
from an index round `n` found, extending that index's path by the step. -/
def searchRound (root : Index) (adjacency : ∀ j : Index, List (Σ p : Index, S.Step p j)) :
    ℕ → ∀ j : Index, Option (Option (Σ p : Index, S.Step p j) × S.Walk root j)
  | 0, j => if same : j = root then some (none, cast (congrArg (S.Walk root) same.symm) (.nil root))
      else none
  | n + 1, j =>
    match searchRound root adjacency n j with
    | some entry => some entry
    | none => (adjacency j).findSome? fun link =>
        (searchRound root adjacency n link.1).map fun entry =>
          (some link, entry.2.append link.2.toWalk)

variable {root : Index} {adjacency : ∀ j : Index, List (Σ p : Index, S.Step p j)}

theorem searchRound_zero_root :
    searchRound root adjacency 0 root = some (none, .nil root) := by
  rw [searchRound, dif_pos rfl]
  rfl

theorem searchRound_succ_of_eq_some {n : ℕ} {j : Index}
    {entry : Option (Σ p : Index, S.Step p j) × S.Walk root j}
    (found : searchRound root adjacency n j = some entry) :
    searchRound root adjacency (n + 1) j = some entry := by
  rw [searchRound, found]

theorem searchRound_succ_of_eq_none {n : ℕ} {j : Index}
    (missing : searchRound root adjacency n j = none) :
    searchRound root adjacency (n + 1) j = (adjacency j).findSome? fun link =>
      (searchRound root adjacency n link.1).map fun entry =>
        (some link, entry.2.append link.2.toWalk) := by
  rw [searchRound, missing]

/-- What a round finds, every later round keeps. -/
theorem searchRound_add {n : ℕ} {j : Index}
    {entry : Option (Σ p : Index, S.Step p j) × S.Walk root j}
    (found : searchRound root adjacency n j = some entry) :
    ∀ k : ℕ, searchRound root adjacency (n + k) j = some entry
  | 0 => found
  | k + 1 => searchRound_succ_of_eq_some (searchRound_add found k)

/-- All rounds that find an index find the same entry. -/
theorem searchRound_unique {m n : ℕ} {j : Index}
    {first second : Option (Σ p : Index, S.Step p j) × S.Walk root j}
    (foundFirst : searchRound root adjacency m j = some first)
    (foundSecond : searchRound root adjacency n j = some second) : first = second := by
  have later := searchRound_add foundFirst n
  have later' := searchRound_add foundSecond m
  rw [Nat.add_comm] at later'
  exact Option.some.inj (later.symm.trans later')

/-- Only the root is found without a parent. -/
theorem eq_root_of_searchRound {n : ℕ} {j : Index} {path : S.Walk root j}
    (found : searchRound root adjacency n j = some (none, path)) : j = root := by
  induction n generalizing j with
  | zero =>
    rw [searchRound] at found
    split at found
    · assumption
    · exact nomatch found
  | succ n ih =>
    cases previous : searchRound root adjacency n j with
    | none =>
      rw [searchRound_succ_of_eq_none previous] at found
      obtain ⟨link, _, extended⟩ := List.exists_of_findSome?_eq_some found
      obtain ⟨_, _, same⟩ := Option.map_eq_some_iff.mp extended
      exact nomatch congrArg Prod.fst same
    | some entry =>
      rw [searchRound_succ_of_eq_some previous] at found
      rw [Option.some.inj found] at previous
      exact ih previous

/-- An index found with a parent extends, by its parent link, a path some round found for the
parent. -/
theorem searchRound_parent {n : ℕ} {j p : Index} {step : S.Step p j} {path : S.Walk root j}
    (found : searchRound root adjacency n j = some (some ⟨p, step⟩, path)) :
    ∃ (m : ℕ) (entry : Option (Σ q : Index, S.Step q p) × S.Walk root p),
      searchRound root adjacency m p = some entry ∧ path = entry.2.append step.toWalk := by
  induction n generalizing j with
  | zero =>
    rw [searchRound] at found
    split at found
    · exact nomatch congrArg Prod.fst (Option.some.inj found)
    · exact nomatch found
  | succ n ih =>
    cases previous : searchRound root adjacency n j with
    | none =>
      rw [searchRound_succ_of_eq_none previous] at found
      obtain ⟨link, _, extended⟩ := List.exists_of_findSome?_eq_some found
      obtain ⟨entry, foundParent, same⟩ := Option.map_eq_some_iff.mp extended
      have linkEq : link = ⟨p, step⟩ := Option.some.inj (congrArg Prod.fst same)
      subst linkEq
      exact ⟨n, entry, foundParent, (congrArg Prod.snd same).symm⟩
    | some entry =>
      rw [searchRound_succ_of_eq_some previous] at found
      rw [Option.some.inj found] at previous
      exact ih previous

/-- A round that finds an index lets the next round find every index one step away. -/
theorem searchRound_isSome_succ
    (complete : ∀ {p j : Index} (step : S.Step p j), ⟨p, step⟩ ∈ adjacency j)
    {n : ℕ} {p j : Index} (step : S.Step p j)
    (reached : (searchRound root adjacency n p).isSome = true) :
    (searchRound root adjacency (n + 1) j).isSome = true := by
  cases previous : searchRound root adjacency n j with
  | some entry => rw [searchRound_succ_of_eq_some previous]; rfl
  | none =>
    rw [searchRound_succ_of_eq_none previous]
    refine List.findSome?_isSome_iff.mpr ⟨⟨p, step⟩, complete step, ?_⟩
    cases foundParent : searchRound root adjacency n p with
    | none => rw [foundParent] at reached; exact nomatch reached
    | some _ => rfl

/-- A walk of length `k` from an index found at round `n` reaches an index found at round
`n + k`. -/
theorem searchRound_isSome_of_walk
    (complete : ∀ {p j : Index} (step : S.Step p j), ⟨p, step⟩ ∈ adjacency j)
    {i j : Index} (walk : S.Walk i j) {n : ℕ}
    (reached : (searchRound root adjacency n i).isSome = true) :
    (searchRound root adjacency (n + walk.length) j).isSome = true := by
  induction walk generalizing n with
  | nil => exact reached
  | forward edge rest ih =>
    have next := ih (searchRound_isSome_succ complete (.forward edge) reached)
    show (searchRound root adjacency (n + (rest.length + 1)) _).isSome = true
    rwa [show n + (rest.length + 1) = n + 1 + rest.length by omega]
  | backward edge rest ih =>
    have next := ih (searchRound_isSome_succ complete (.backward edge) reached)
    show (searchRound root adjacency (n + (rest.length + 1)) _).isSome = true
    rwa [show n + (rest.length + 1) = n + 1 + rest.length by omega]

/-- A walk from the root reaches an index found at the round of its length. -/
theorem searchRound_isSome_of_walk_root
    (complete : ∀ {p j : Index} (step : S.Step p j), ⟨p, step⟩ ∈ adjacency j)
    {j : Index} (walk : S.Walk root j) :
    (searchRound root adjacency walk.length j).isSome = true := by
  have reached := searchRound_isSome_of_walk (adjacency := adjacency) complete walk
    (n := 0) (by rw [searchRound_zero_root]; rfl)
  rwa [Nat.zero_add] at reached

variable (adjacency) in
/-- **The entry of an index**: what the round given by the length of a walk from the root finds.
Every such walk gives the same entry, so a merely given walk suffices. -/
def searchEntry (complete : ∀ {p j : Index} (step : S.Step p j), ⟨p, step⟩ ∈ adjacency j)
    (connect : ∀ j : Index, Trunc (S.Walk root j)) (j : Index) :
    Option (Σ p : Index, S.Step p j) × S.Walk root j :=
  Trunc.lift
    (fun walk : S.Walk root j =>
      (searchRound root adjacency walk.length j).get
        (searchRound_isSome_of_walk_root complete walk))
    (fun _ _ => searchRound_unique (Option.eq_some_of_isSome _) (Option.eq_some_of_isSome _))
    (connect j)

theorem searchEntry_spec
    (complete : ∀ {p j : Index} (step : S.Step p j), ⟨p, step⟩ ∈ adjacency j)
    (connect : ∀ j : Index, Trunc (S.Walk root j)) (j : Index) :
    ∃ n, searchRound root adjacency n j = some (searchEntry adjacency complete connect j) :=
  Trunc.induction_on
    (β := fun walk => ∃ n, searchRound root adjacency n j = some (Trunc.lift
      (fun walk : S.Walk root j => (searchRound root adjacency walk.length j).get
        (searchRound_isSome_of_walk_root complete walk))
      (fun _ _ =>
        searchRound_unique (Option.eq_some_of_isSome _) (Option.eq_some_of_isSome _)) walk))
    (connect j) fun walk => ⟨walk.length, Option.eq_some_of_isSome _⟩

variable (adjacency) in
/-- **A spanning tree built in rounds**, for a connected, locally finite index graph whose indices
have decidable equality: each index hangs from the parent through which a round first found it.
No choice is involved. -/
def SpanningTree.ofRounds
    (complete : ∀ {p j : Index} (step : S.Step p j), ⟨p, step⟩ ∈ adjacency j)
    (connect : ∀ j : Index, Trunc (S.Walk root j)) : S.SpanningTree root where
  parent j := (searchEntry adjacency complete connect j).1
  path j := (searchEntry adjacency complete connect j).2
  path_root := by
    obtain ⟨_, found⟩ := searchEntry_spec complete connect root
    rw [searchRound_unique found searchRound_zero_root]
  eq_root j missing := by
    obtain ⟨n, found⟩ := searchEntry_spec complete connect j
    exact eq_root_of_searchRound (n := n) (path := (searchEntry adjacency complete connect j).2)
      (by rw [found, ← missing])
  path_parent j p step linked := by
    obtain ⟨n, found⟩ := searchEntry_spec complete connect j
    obtain ⟨m, entry, foundParent, extended⟩ := searchRound_parent (n := n)
      (path := (searchEntry adjacency complete connect j).2) (by rw [found, ← linked])
    obtain ⟨_, foundParent'⟩ := searchEntry_spec complete connect p
    rw [extended, searchRound_unique foundParent foundParent']

/-- The steps into an index, read off a list of edges. -/
def adjacencyOfEdges (edges : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)) (j : Index) :
    List (Σ p : Index, S.Step p j) :=
  edges.flatMap fun edge =>
    (if same : edge.2.1 = j then
      [⟨edge.1, .forward (cast (congrArg (S.Edge edge.1) same) edge.2.2)⟩] else []) ++
    (if same : edge.1 = j then
      [⟨edge.2.1, .backward (cast (congrArg (fun i => S.Edge i edge.2.1) same) edge.2.2)⟩]
      else [])

/-- A complete list of edges lists every step into every index. -/
theorem mem_adjacencyOfEdges {edges : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)}
    (complete : ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j), ⟨i, j, edge⟩ ∈ edges)
    {p j : Index} (step : S.Step p j) : ⟨p, step⟩ ∈ adjacencyOfEdges edges j := by
  cases step with
  | forward edge =>
    refine List.mem_flatMap.mpr ⟨⟨p, j, edge⟩, complete edge, List.mem_append_left _ ?_⟩
    rw [dif_pos rfl]
    exact List.mem_singleton_self _
  | backward edge =>
    refine List.mem_flatMap.mpr ⟨⟨j, p, edge⟩, complete edge, List.mem_append_right _ ?_⟩
    rw [dif_pos rfl]
    exact List.mem_singleton_self _

end Rounds

/-! ## Enumerating closed walks -/

section ClosedWalks

/-- A step followed by a walk. -/
def Step.prepend {i j k : Index} : S.Step i j → S.Walk j k → S.Walk i k
  | .forward edge, rest => .forward edge rest
  | .backward edge, rest => .backward edge rest

/-- **Read a list of ranks as a walk** from an index: each rank picks one of the listed steps out
of the current index. -/
def walkOfRanks (outSteps : ∀ i : Index, List (Σ j : Index, S.Step i j)) :
    (i : Index) → List ℕ → Option (Σ j : Index, S.Walk i j)
  | i, [] => some ⟨i, .nil i⟩
  | i, rank :: ranks =>
    match (outSteps i)[rank]? with
    | none => none
    | some ⟨_, step⟩ =>
      (walkOfRanks outSteps _ ranks).map fun found => ⟨found.1, step.prepend found.2⟩

/-- **Every walk is read from some list of ranks** when the steps out of every index are listed. -/
theorem exists_walkOfRanks {outSteps : ∀ i : Index, List (Σ j : Index, S.Step i j)}
    (complete : ∀ {i j : Index} (step : S.Step i j), ⟨j, step⟩ ∈ outSteps i)
    {i j : Index} (walk : S.Walk i j) :
    ∃ ranks, walkOfRanks outSteps i ranks = some ⟨j, walk⟩ := by
  induction walk with
  | nil i => exact ⟨[], rfl⟩
  | @forward i k j edge rest ih =>
    obtain ⟨ranks, read⟩ := ih
    obtain ⟨rank, at_⟩ := List.mem_iff_getElem?.mp (complete (.forward edge))
    refine ⟨rank :: ranks, ?_⟩
    rw [walkOfRanks, at_]
    show Option.map _ (walkOfRanks outSteps k ranks) = _
    rw [read]
    rfl
  | @backward i k j edge rest ih =>
    obtain ⟨ranks, read⟩ := ih
    obtain ⟨rank, at_⟩ := List.mem_iff_getElem?.mp (complete (.backward edge))
    refine ⟨rank :: ranks, ?_⟩
    rw [walkOfRanks, at_]
    show Option.map _ (walkOfRanks outSteps k ranks) = _
    rw [read]
    rfl

variable [DecidableEq Index]

/-- **The closed walks at an index, enumerated** through the lists of ranks. -/
def closedWalkOfRank (outSteps : ∀ i : Index, List (Σ j : Index, S.Step i j)) (root : Index)
    (stage : ℕ) : Option (S.Walk root root) :=
  match walkOfRanks outSteps root (listOfRank stage) with
  | some ⟨k, walk⟩ =>
    if same : k = root then some (cast (congrArg (S.Walk root) same) walk) else none
  | none => none

/-- **Every closed walk occurs** at some rank, when the steps out of every index are listed. -/
theorem exists_closedWalkOfRank_eq {outSteps : ∀ i : Index, List (Σ j : Index, S.Step i j)}
    (complete : ∀ {i j : Index} (step : S.Step i j), ⟨j, step⟩ ∈ outSteps i) {root : Index}
    (loop : S.Walk root root) : ∃ stage, closedWalkOfRank outSteps root stage = some loop := by
  obtain ⟨ranks, read⟩ := exists_walkOfRanks complete loop
  obtain ⟨stage, at_⟩ := exists_listOfRank_eq ranks
  refine ⟨stage, ?_⟩
  unfold closedWalkOfRank
  rw [at_, read]
  show (if same : root = root then some (cast (congrArg (S.Walk root) same) loop) else none) = _
  rw [dif_pos rfl]
  rfl

/-- The steps out of an index, read off a list of edges. -/
def outStepsOfEdges (edges : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)) (i : Index) :
    List (Σ j : Index, S.Step i j) :=
  edges.flatMap fun edge =>
    (if same : edge.1 = i then
      [⟨edge.2.1,
        .forward (cast (congrArg (fun source => S.Edge source edge.2.1) same) edge.2.2)⟩]
      else []) ++
    (if same : edge.2.1 = i then
      [⟨edge.1, .backward (cast (congrArg (S.Edge edge.1) same) edge.2.2)⟩] else [])

/-- A complete list of edges lists every step out of every index. -/
theorem mem_outStepsOfEdges {edges : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)}
    (complete : ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j), ⟨i, j, edge⟩ ∈ edges)
    {i j : Index} (step : S.Step i j) : ⟨j, step⟩ ∈ outStepsOfEdges edges i := by
  cases step with
  | forward edge =>
    refine List.mem_flatMap.mpr ⟨⟨i, j, edge⟩, complete edge, List.mem_append_left _ ?_⟩
    rw [dif_pos rfl]
    exact List.mem_singleton_self _
  | backward edge =>
    refine List.mem_flatMap.mpr ⟨⟨j, i, edge⟩, complete edge, List.mem_append_right _ ?_⟩
    rw [dif_pos rfl]
    exact List.mem_singleton_self _

/-- **Fair search over a locally finite index graph**: when the steps out of every index are
listed and the view at the root is enumerated, the dovetailed schedule of the closed walks at the
root and the values is fair. -/
theorem dovetail_closedWalks_fair {outSteps : ∀ i : Index, List (Σ j : Index, S.Step i j)}
    (complete : ∀ {i j : Index} (step : S.Step i j), ⟨j, step⟩ ∈ outSteps i) {root : Index}
    {values : ℕ → Option (S.View root)}
    (listsValues : ∀ value, ∃ rank, values rank = some value) :
    Fair (dovetail (closedWalkOfRank outSteps root) values) :=
  dovetail_fair (exists_closedWalkOfRank_eq complete) listsValues

end ClosedWalks

/-! ## A certified decision procedure for finite systems -/

namespace SpanningTree

variable {root : Index} (T : S.SpanningTree root)

/-- The chords among a list of edges: the edges outside the tree. -/
def chordList [DecidableEq Index] [∀ i j : Index, DecidableEq (S.Edge i j)]
    (edges : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)) : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j) :=
  edges.filter fun edge => !decide (T.IsTreeEdge edge.2.2)

theorem mem_chordList [DecidableEq Index] [∀ i j : Index, DecidableEq (S.Edge i j)]
    {edges : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)}
    (complete : ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j), ⟨i, j, edge⟩ ∈ edges)
    {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j) (chord : ¬ T.IsTreeEdge edge) :
    ⟨i, j, edge⟩ ∈ T.chordList edges :=
  List.mem_filter.mpr ⟨complete edge, by rw [decide_eq_false chord]; rfl⟩

/-- **The search over fundamental cycles**: the first listed chord and listed value whose
fundamental cycle moves the value. -/
def search [DecidableEq (S.View root)] (chords : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j))
    (values : List (S.View root)) : Option T.CycleDisparity :=
  chords.findSome? fun chord => values.findSome? fun value =>
    if fixed : S.transport (T.cycle chord.2.2) value = value then none
    else some ⟨chord.1, chord.2.1, chord.2.2, value, fixed⟩

theorem search_eq_none_iff [DecidableEq (S.View root)] {chords : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)}
    {values : List (S.View root)} :
    T.search chords values = none ↔
      ∀ chord ∈ chords, ∀ value ∈ values,
        S.transport (T.cycle chord.2.2) value = value := by
  constructor
  · intro missing chord member value memberValue
    have inner := List.findSome?_eq_none_iff.mp
      (List.findSome?_eq_none_iff.mp missing chord member) value memberValue
    exact if fixed : S.transport (T.cycle chord.2.2) value = value then fixed
      else by rw [dif_neg fixed] at inner; exact nomatch inner
  · intro fixed
    refine List.findSome?_eq_none_iff.mpr fun chord member => ?_
    refine List.findSome?_eq_none_iff.mpr fun value memberValue => ?_
    rw [dif_pos (fixed chord member value memberValue)]

/-- When the search over a list containing every chord and a listing of the view at the root finds
nothing, holonomy at the root is trivial. -/
theorem trivialHolonomyAt_of_search_eq_none [DecidableEq (S.View root)]
    {chords : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)} {values : List (S.View root)}
    (chordsComplete : ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j), ¬ T.IsTreeEdge edge →
      ⟨i, j, edge⟩ ∈ chords)
    (valuesComplete : ∀ value : S.View root, value ∈ values)
    (searched : T.search chords values = none) : S.TrivialHolonomyAt root :=
  T.trivialHolonomyAt_iff_chords.mpr fun edge chord value =>
    T.search_eq_none_iff.mp searched ⟨_, _, edge⟩ (chordsComplete edge chord) value
      (valuesComplete value)

/-- **The search is exact**: it finds nothing exactly when holonomy at the root is trivial. -/
theorem search_eq_none_iff_trivialHolonomyAt [DecidableEq (S.View root)]
    {chords : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)} {values : List (S.View root)}
    (chordsComplete : ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j), ¬ T.IsTreeEdge edge →
      ⟨i, j, edge⟩ ∈ chords)
    (valuesComplete : ∀ value : S.View root, value ∈ values) :
    T.search chords values = none ↔ S.TrivialHolonomyAt root := by
  refine ⟨T.trivialHolonomyAt_of_search_eq_none chordsComplete valuesComplete,
    fun trivial => ?_⟩
  cases found : T.search chords values with
  | none => rfl
  | some disparity => exact absurd (trivial _ _) disparity.toDisparityAt.moved

/-- **The decision procedure**: search the fundamental cycles of the listed chords against the
listed values.  It refutes gluing with the disparity it finds, or establishes gluing with the
gluing built from trivial holonomy along the tree; it is never outside its fragment and never
incomplete. -/
def gluingVerdict [DecidableEq (S.View root)] (chords : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j))
    (values : List (S.View root))
    (chordsComplete : ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j), ¬ T.IsTreeEdge edge →
      ⟨i, j, edge⟩ ∈ chords)
    (valuesComplete : ∀ value : S.View root, value ∈ values) :
    Outcome S.Gluing T.CycleDisparity Empty Empty :=
  match searched : T.search chords values with
  | some disparity => .refuted disparity
  | none => .established (gluingOfTrivialHolonomy
      ((trivialHolonomy_iff_at T.connect).mpr
        (T.trivialHolonomyAt_of_search_eq_none chordsComplete valuesComplete searched))
      T.connect)

section Verdict

variable [DecidableEq (S.View root)] {chords : List (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)}
  {values : List (S.View root)}
  (chordsComplete : ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j), ¬ T.IsTreeEdge edge →
    ⟨i, j, edge⟩ ∈ chords)
  (valuesComplete : ∀ value : S.View root, value ∈ values)

theorem gluingVerdict_isDecided :
    (T.gluingVerdict chords values chordsComplete valuesComplete).isDecided = true := by
  unfold gluingVerdict
  split <;> rfl

/-- **Correct for gluing**: the procedure establishes gluing exactly when the views glue. -/
theorem gluingVerdict_asBool_eq_true_iff :
    (T.gluingVerdict chords values chordsComplete valuesComplete).asBool = some true ↔
      Nonempty S.Gluing := by
  unfold gluingVerdict
  split
  · rename_i disparity _
    exact ⟨(fun answer => nomatch answer),
      fun glues => absurd glues (Disparity.not_gluing ⟨root, disparity.toDisparityAt⟩)⟩
  · rename_i searched
    exact ⟨fun _ => ⟨gluingOfTrivialHolonomy ((trivialHolonomy_iff_at T.connect).mpr
        (T.trivialHolonomyAt_of_search_eq_none chordsComplete valuesComplete searched))
        T.connect⟩, fun _ => rfl⟩

/-- **Correct for disparity**: the procedure refutes gluing exactly when the register is
inhabited. -/
theorem gluingVerdict_asBool_eq_false_iff :
    (T.gluingVerdict chords values chordsComplete valuesComplete).asBool = some false ↔
      Nonempty S.Disparity := by
  unfold gluingVerdict
  split
  · rename_i disparity _
    exact ⟨fun _ => ⟨⟨root, disparity.toDisparityAt⟩⟩, fun _ => rfl⟩
  · rename_i searched
    exact ⟨(fun answer => nomatch answer), fun ⟨disparity⟩ => absurd
      ⟨gluingOfTrivialHolonomy ((trivialHolonomy_iff_at T.connect).mpr
        (T.trivialHolonomyAt_of_search_eq_none chordsComplete valuesComplete searched))
        T.connect⟩ disparity.not_gluing⟩

/-- **A refutation is a certificate**: the disparity it returns is a disparity at a fundamental
cycle, so the views do not glue. -/
theorem not_gluing_of_gluingVerdict_eq_refuted {disparity : T.CycleDisparity}
    (_ : T.gluingVerdict chords values chordsComplete valuesComplete = .refuted disparity) :
    ¬ Nonempty S.Gluing :=
  Disparity.not_gluing ⟨root, disparity.toDisparityAt⟩

/-- **Gluing is decidable** for a system with a spanning tree, a list containing its chords, and
a listing of the view at the root with decidable equality. -/
def decidableNonemptyGluing : Decidable (Nonempty S.Gluing) :=
  decidable_of_iff _ (T.gluingVerdict_asBool_eq_true_iff chordsComplete valuesComplete)

end Verdict

end SpanningTree

section Finite

variable [DecidableEq Index] [∀ i j : Index, DecidableEq (S.Edge i j)] {root : Index}

/-- The spanning tree built in rounds from a listing of the edges. -/
def SpanningTree.ofEdges (edges : Listing (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j))
    (connect : ∀ j : Index, Trunc (S.Walk root j)) : S.SpanningTree root :=
  SpanningTree.ofRounds (adjacencyOfEdges edges.elems)
    (mem_adjacencyOfEdges fun edge => edges.complete ⟨_, _, edge⟩) connect

variable [DecidableEq (S.View root)]

/-- **The decision procedure for a finite connected system**: build a spanning tree in rounds from
a listing of the edges, list its chords, and search their fundamental cycles against a listing of
the view at the root. -/
def finiteGluingVerdict (edges : Listing (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j))
    (values : Listing (S.View root)) (connect : ∀ j : Index, Trunc (S.Walk root j)) :
    Outcome S.Gluing (SpanningTree.ofEdges edges connect).CycleDisparity Empty Empty :=
  (SpanningTree.ofEdges edges connect).gluingVerdict
    ((SpanningTree.ofEdges edges connect).chordList edges.elems) values.elems
    (fun edge chord => (SpanningTree.ofEdges edges connect).mem_chordList
      (fun edge => edges.complete ⟨_, _, edge⟩) edge chord)
    values.complete

theorem finiteGluingVerdict_asBool_eq_true_iff (edges : Listing (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j))
    (values : Listing (S.View root)) (connect : ∀ j : Index, Trunc (S.Walk root j)) :
    (finiteGluingVerdict edges values connect).asBool = some true ↔ Nonempty S.Gluing :=
  (SpanningTree.ofEdges edges connect).gluingVerdict_asBool_eq_true_iff
    (fun edge chord => (SpanningTree.ofEdges edges connect).mem_chordList
      (fun edge => edges.complete ⟨_, _, edge⟩) edge chord)
    values.complete

theorem finiteGluingVerdict_asBool_eq_false_iff (edges : Listing (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j))
    (values : Listing (S.View root)) (connect : ∀ j : Index, Trunc (S.Walk root j)) :
    (finiteGluingVerdict edges values connect).asBool = some false ↔ Nonempty S.Disparity :=
  (SpanningTree.ofEdges edges connect).gluingVerdict_asBool_eq_false_iff
    (fun edge chord => (SpanningTree.ofEdges edges connect).mem_chordList
      (fun edge => edges.complete ⟨_, _, edge⟩) edge chord)
    values.complete

/-- Gluing is decidable for a finite connected system given by listings. -/
def decidableNonemptyGluingOfListings (edges : Listing (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j))
    (values : Listing (S.View root)) (connect : ∀ j : Index, Trunc (S.Walk root j)) :
    Decidable (Nonempty S.Gluing) :=
  decidable_of_iff _ (finiteGluingVerdict_asBool_eq_true_iff edges values connect)

/-- **Gluing is decidable for a finite connected system given by `Fintype` instances**: the
listings are merely given and the answer does not depend on them.  This version inherits
classical choice from membership in the library's finite sets; the listing versions do not use
choice. -/
def decidableNonemptyGluingOfFintype [Fintype (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)]
    [Fintype (S.View root)] (connect : ∀ j : Index, Trunc (S.Walk root j)) :
    Decidable (Nonempty S.Gluing) :=
  Trunc.lift
    (fun edges => Trunc.lift
      (fun values => decidableNonemptyGluingOfListings edges values connect)
      (fun _ _ => Subsingleton.elim _ _) (Listing.ofFintype (S.View root)))
    (fun _ _ => Subsingleton.elim _ _) (Listing.ofFintype (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j))

end Finite

/-! ## Fair search without decidable equality -/

section Search

variable {root : Index}

variable (S root) in
/-- **A disparity witnessed by apartness** at the root: a closed walk and a value it moves apart.
This is what a finite search can confirm. -/
structure ApartDisparity (apartness : SemiApartness (S.View root)) where
  /-- The closed walk. -/
  loop : S.Walk root root
  /-- The value it moves. -/
  value : S.View root
  apart : apartness.Apart (S.transport loop value) value

variable {apartness : SemiApartness (S.View root)}

/-- A disparity witnessed by apartness is a disparity. -/
def ApartDisparity.toDisparityAt (disparity : S.ApartDisparity root apartness) :
    S.DisparityAt root :=
  ⟨disparity.loop, disparity.value, apartness.ne_of_apart disparity.apart⟩

/-- When distinctness implies apartness, every disparity is witnessed by apartness.  Decidable
equality gives this implication; for boolean streams it is a classical step. -/
def ApartDisparity.ofDisparityAt (tight : ∀ {a b : S.View root}, a ≠ b → apartness.Apart a b)
    (disparity : S.DisparityAt root) : S.ApartDisparity root apartness :=
  ⟨disparity.loop, disparity.value, tight disparity.moved⟩

variable (apartness) in
/-- **The examination at a stage** of a schedule of closed walks and values with budgets: it
reports when the test confirms, within the budget, that the walk moves the value apart. -/
def examine (schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ)) (stage : ℕ) :
    Option (S.ApartDisparity root apartness) :=
  match schedule stage with
  | some ((loop, value), budget) =>
    if confirmed : apartness.test (S.transport loop value) value budget = true then
      some ⟨loop, value, apartness.test_sound confirmed⟩
    else none
  | none => none

theorem examine_of_scheduled {schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ)}
    {stage : ℕ} {loop : S.Walk root root} {value : S.View root} {budget : ℕ}
    (scheduled : schedule stage = some ((loop, value), budget))
    (confirmed : apartness.test (S.transport loop value) value budget = true) :
    examine apartness schedule stage = some ⟨loop, value, apartness.test_sound confirmed⟩ := by
  unfold examine
  rw [scheduled]
  exact dif_pos confirmed

/-- **Soundness**: nothing is reported without a certificate.  A report names the closed walk and
the value examined at its stage, with a budget at which the test confirms that they are apart. -/
theorem examine_sound {schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ)}
    {stage : ℕ} {disparity : S.ApartDisparity root apartness}
    (reported : examine apartness schedule stage = some disparity) :
    ∃ budget, schedule stage = some ((disparity.loop, disparity.value), budget) ∧
      apartness.test (S.transport disparity.loop disparity.value) disparity.value budget =
        true := by
  unfold examine at reported
  split at reported
  · rename_i loop value budget scheduled
    split at reported
    · rename_i confirmed
      cases reported
      exact ⟨budget, scheduled, confirmed⟩
    · exact nomatch reported
  · exact nomatch reported

/-- **Completeness under fairness**: a fair schedule reports every disparity witnessed by
apartness at some finite stage. -/
theorem examine_complete {schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ)}
    (fair : Fair schedule) (disparity : S.ApartDisparity root apartness) :
    ∃ stage, examine apartness schedule stage = some disparity := by
  obtain ⟨budget, confirmed⟩ := apartness.test_complete disparity.apart
  obtain ⟨stage, budget', le, scheduled⟩ := fair (disparity.loop, disparity.value) budget
  exact ⟨stage, examine_of_scheduled scheduled (apartness.test_mono le confirmed)⟩

/-- **The dovetailed search reports every disparity witnessed by apartness whose closed walk and
value are listed**, at some finite stage, whatever budget its confirmation needs. -/
theorem examine_dovetail {loops : ℕ → Option (S.Walk root root)}
    {values : ℕ → Option (S.View root)} (disparity : S.ApartDisparity root apartness)
    (listedLoop : ∃ r, loops r = some disparity.loop)
    (listedValue : ∃ s, values s = some disparity.value) :
    ∃ stage, examine apartness (dovetail loops values) stage = some disparity := by
  obtain ⟨budget, confirmed⟩ := apartness.test_complete disparity.apart
  obtain ⟨_, listedLoop⟩ := listedLoop
  obtain ⟨_, listedValue⟩ := listedValue
  obtain ⟨stage, scheduled⟩ := dovetail_examines listedLoop listedValue budget
  exact ⟨stage, examine_of_scheduled scheduled confirmed⟩

/-- **The register is semi-decidable**: under a fair schedule, some stage reports exactly when a
disparity witnessed by apartness exists. -/
theorem exists_examine_iff {schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ)}
    (fair : Fair schedule) :
    (∃ stage, (examine apartness schedule stage).isSome = true) ↔
      Nonempty (S.ApartDisparity root apartness) := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨stage, reported⟩
    exact ⟨(examine apartness schedule stage).get reported⟩
  · rintro ⟨disparity⟩
    obtain ⟨stage, reported⟩ := examine_complete fair disparity
    exact ⟨stage, by rw [reported]; rfl⟩

/-- **Every disparity is eventually confirmed** when distinctness implies apartness. -/
theorem examine_complete_of_tight
    {schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ)} (fair : Fair schedule)
    (tight : ∀ {a b : S.View root}, a ≠ b → apartness.Apart a b)
    (disparity : S.DisparityAt root) :
    ∃ stage, examine apartness schedule stage =
      some (ApartDisparity.ofDisparityAt tight disparity) :=
  examine_complete fair _

variable (apartness) in
/-- The first report among the first `stages` stages. -/
def firstReport (schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ))
    (stages : ℕ) : Option (S.ApartDisparity root apartness) :=
  (List.range stages).findSome? (examine apartness schedule)

variable (apartness) in
/-- **The budgeted verdict on gluing** after a number of stages: refuted by the first reported
disparity, and otherwise incomplete, with the stages spent as its receipt.  A finite search never
establishes gluing. -/
def searchVerdict (schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ))
    (stages : ℕ) : Outcome S.Gluing (S.ApartDisparity root apartness) Empty ℕ :=
  match firstReport apartness schedule stages with
  | some disparity => .refuted disparity
  | none => .incomplete stages

theorem firstReport_add {schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ)}
    {stages : ℕ} {disparity : S.ApartDisparity root apartness}
    (found : firstReport apartness schedule stages = some disparity) (extra : ℕ) :
    firstReport apartness schedule (stages + extra) = some disparity := by
  unfold firstReport at found ⊢
  rw [List.range_add, List.findSome?_append, found]
  rfl

/-- **Budgets only refine the verdict**: more stages can turn an incomplete verdict into a
refutation, and never change a refutation. -/
theorem searchVerdict_budget_mono
    {schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ)} {small large : ℕ}
    (le : small ≤ large) :
    Outcome.BudgetRefines (searchVerdict apartness schedule small)
      (searchVerdict apartness schedule large) := by
  obtain ⟨extra, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_le le
  unfold searchVerdict
  cases found : firstReport apartness schedule small with
  | some disparity =>
    rw [firstReport_add found extra]
    exact .refuted disparity disparity
  | none =>
    cases firstReport apartness schedule (small + extra) with
    | some disparity => exact .incompleteRefuted small disparity
    | none => exact .incomplete small (small + extra)

/-- A finite search never establishes gluing. -/
theorem searchVerdict_ne_established
    (schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ)) (stages : ℕ)
    (gluing : S.Gluing) : searchVerdict apartness schedule stages ≠ .established gluing := by
  unfold searchVerdict
  split <;> exact fun equal => nomatch equal

/-- **A refutation is a certificate**: the views do not glue. -/
theorem not_gluing_of_searchVerdict_eq_refuted
    {schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ)} {stages : ℕ}
    {disparity : S.ApartDisparity root apartness}
    (_ : searchVerdict apartness schedule stages = .refuted disparity) : ¬ Nonempty S.Gluing :=
  Disparity.not_gluing ⟨root, disparity.toDisparityAt⟩

/-- **Completeness of the verdict under fairness**: if a disparity witnessed by apartness exists,
some number of stages refutes gluing. -/
theorem exists_searchVerdict_refuted
    {schedule : ℕ → Option ((S.Walk root root × S.View root) × ℕ)} (fair : Fair schedule)
    (disparity : S.ApartDisparity root apartness) :
    ∃ stages, (searchVerdict apartness schedule stages).asBool = some false := by
  obtain ⟨stage, reported⟩ := examine_complete fair disparity
  refine ⟨stage + 1, ?_⟩
  unfold searchVerdict
  cases first : firstReport apartness schedule (stage + 1) with
  | some _ => rfl
  | none =>
    exfalso
    unfold firstReport at first
    have missing := List.findSome?_eq_none_iff.mp first stage
      (List.mem_range.mpr (Nat.lt_succ_self stage))
    rw [reported] at missing
    exact nomatch missing

/-- **Fundamental cycles generate the disparities witnessed by a cotransitive apartness**, without
decidable equality: if a walk closed through the tree moves a value apart, some fundamental cycle
moves some value apart. -/
theorem SpanningTree.exists_cycle_apart_of_close (T : S.SpanningTree root)
    (cotransitive : apartness.Cotransitive) {i j : Index} (walk : S.Walk i j)
    (value : S.View root) (moved : apartness.Apart (S.transport (T.close walk) value) value) :
    ∃ (source target : Index) (edge : S.Edge source target) (point : S.View root),
      apartness.Apart (S.transport (T.cycle edge) point) point := by
  induction walk generalizing value with
  | nil i =>
    rw [T.transport_close_nil] at moved
    exact absurd rfl (apartness.ne_of_apart moved)
  | forward edge rest ih =>
    rw [T.transport_close_forward] at moved
    rcases cotransitive.cotrans (S.transport (T.cycle edge) value) moved with later | here
    · exact ih _ later
    · exact ⟨_, _, edge, value, here⟩
  | backward edge rest ih =>
    rw [T.transport_close_backward] at moved
    rcases cotransitive.cotrans (S.transport (T.cycle edge).reverse value) moved with later | here
    · exact ih _ later
    · refine ⟨_, _, edge, S.transport (T.cycle edge).reverse value, ?_⟩
      rw [transport_reverse_right]
      exact cotransitive.symm here

/-- **Every disparity witnessed by a cotransitive apartness yields one at a fundamental cycle.** -/
theorem SpanningTree.exists_cycle_apart (T : S.SpanningTree root)
    (cotransitive : apartness.Cotransitive) (disparity : S.ApartDisparity root apartness) :
    ∃ (source target : Index) (edge : S.Edge source target) (point : S.View root),
      apartness.Apart (S.transport (T.cycle edge) point) point :=
  T.exists_cycle_apart_of_close cotransitive disparity.loop disparity.value
    ((T.transport_close_root disparity.loop disparity.value).symm ▸ disparity.apart)

/-- The fundamental cycles of a sequence of edges. -/
def SpanningTree.cycleOfRank (T : S.SpanningTree root)
    (edges : ℕ → Option (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)) (rank : ℕ) :
    Option (S.Walk root root) :=
  (edges rank).map fun edge => T.cycle edge.2.2

/-- **The dovetailed search over fundamental cycles is complete without decidable equality**:
enumerating the edges and the view at the root, the dovetailed examination of fundamental cycles
and values reports a disparity at some finite stage whenever a disparity witnessed by a
cotransitive apartness exists at the root. -/
theorem SpanningTree.exists_examine_cycles (T : S.SpanningTree root)
    (cotransitive : apartness.Cotransitive) {edges : ℕ → Option (Σ i j : Index, S.Edge i j)}
    (listsEdges : ∀ {i j : Index} (edge : S.Edge i j),
      ∃ rank, edges rank = some ⟨i, j, edge⟩)
    {values : ℕ → Option (S.View root)}
    (listsValues : ∀ value, ∃ rank, values rank = some value)
    (disparity : S.ApartDisparity root apartness) :
    ∃ stage, (examine apartness (dovetail (T.cycleOfRank edges) values) stage).isSome = true := by
  obtain ⟨_, _, edge, point, moved⟩ := T.exists_cycle_apart cotransitive disparity
  obtain ⟨rank, listed⟩ := listsEdges edge
  obtain ⟨stage, reported⟩ := examine_dovetail (loops := T.cycleOfRank edges) (values := values)
    ⟨T.cycle edge, point, moved⟩ ⟨rank, by rw [SpanningTree.cycleOfRank, listed]; rfl⟩
    (listsValues point)
  exact ⟨stage, by rw [reported]; rfl⟩

end Search

end ViewSystem

/-! ## Schedules that are not fair -/

namespace DisparitySearch

/-- **Walks first, values never**: stage `n` examines the `n`-th item of the first sequence with
only the first item of the second, at budget `n`. -/
def firstValueOnly {α : Type u} {β : Type v} (first : ℕ → Option α)
    (second : ℕ → Option β) (stage : ℕ) : Option ((α × β) × ℕ) :=
  match first stage, second 0 with
  | some a, some b => some ((a, b), stage)
  | _, _ => none

theorem firstValueOnly_second {α : Type u} {β : Type v} {first : ℕ → Option α}
    {second : ℕ → Option β} {stage : ℕ} {a : α} {b : β} {budget : ℕ}
    (scheduled : firstValueOnly first second stage = some ((a, b), budget)) :
    second 0 = some b := by
  unfold firstValueOnly at scheduled
  split at scheduled
  · rename_i listedSecond
    cases scheduled
    exact listedSecond
  · exact nomatch scheduled

/-- **A fixed budget**: the dovetailed pairs, every one at budget `0`. -/
def zeroBudget {α : Type u} {β : Type v} (first : ℕ → Option α) (second : ℕ → Option β)
    (stage : ℕ) : Option ((α × β) × ℕ) :=
  (dovetail first second stage).map fun examined => (examined.1, 0)

theorem zeroBudget_budget {α : Type u} {β : Type v} {first : ℕ → Option α}
    {second : ℕ → Option β} {stage : ℕ} {item : α × β} {budget : ℕ}
    (scheduled : zeroBudget first second stage = some (item, budget)) : budget = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨_, _, same⟩ := Option.map_eq_some_iff.mp scheduled
  exact (congrArg Prod.snd same).symm

end DisparitySearch

/-! ## Controls -/

namespace Twisted

open ViewSystem DisparitySearch

instance twistedEdgeDecidableEq (i j : Vertex) : DecidableEq (twisted.Edge i j) :=
  fun first second => isTrue (by
    change CycleEdge i j at first second
    cases first <;> cases second <;> rfl)

instance twistedViewDecidableEq (j : Vertex) : DecidableEq (twisted.View j) :=
  inferInstanceAs (DecidableEq Bool)

/-- **The spanning tree of the twisted cycle** at `a`: `b` hangs from `a` along `ab` and `c` from
`b` along `bc`, so `ca` is the only chord. -/
def tree : twisted.SpanningTree Vertex.a where
  parent
    | .a => none
    | .b => some ⟨.a, .forward CycleEdge.ab⟩
    | .c => some ⟨.b, .forward CycleEdge.bc⟩
  path
    | .a => .nil _
    | .b => .forward CycleEdge.ab (.nil _)
    | .c => .forward CycleEdge.ab (.forward CycleEdge.bc (.nil _))
  path_root := rfl
  eq_root
    | .a, _ => rfl
    | .b, missing => nomatch missing
    | .c, missing => nomatch missing
  path_parent
    | .a, _, _, linked => nomatch linked
    | .b, _, _, linked => by cases linked; rfl
    | .c, _, _, linked => by cases linked; rfl

/-- The three edges of the twisted cycle. -/
def edgeListing : Listing (Σ i j : Vertex, twisted.Edge i j) where
  elems := [⟨.a, .b, CycleEdge.ab⟩, ⟨.b, .c, CycleEdge.bc⟩, ⟨.c, .a, CycleEdge.ca⟩]
  complete := fun ⟨i, j, edge⟩ => by
    change CycleEdge i j at edge
    cases edge
    · exact List.Mem.head _
    · exact List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _)
    · exact List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _))

/-- The two booleans. -/
def boolListing : Listing Bool where
  elems := [false, true]
  complete
    | false => List.Mem.head _
    | true => List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _)

/-- **The fundamental cycle of the tree edge `ab` is trivial.** -/
theorem tree_cycle_ab (value : Bool) :
    twisted.transport (tree.cycle CycleEdge.ab) value = value :=
  tree.transport_cycle_of_isTreeEdge (Or.inl rfl) value

/-- **The fundamental cycle of the chord `ca` is the twist**: it negates every value. -/
theorem tree_cycle_ca (value : Bool) :
    twisted.transport (tree.cycle CycleEdge.ca) value = !value := by
  cases value <;> rfl

/-- **The only chord is `ca`.** -/
theorem tree_chordList : tree.chordList edgeListing.elems = [⟨.c, .a, CycleEdge.ca⟩] :=
  rfl

/-- **The search finds the disparity at the one fundamental cycle**: the chord `ca` moves
`false`. -/
theorem tree_search :
    tree.search (tree.chordList edgeListing.elems) boolListing.elems =
      some ⟨.c, .a, CycleEdge.ca, false,
        fun fixed => absurd (show (true : Bool) = false from fixed) (by decide)⟩ :=
  rfl

/-- **The decision procedure refutes gluing**, with the disparity at the chord `ca` as its
certificate. -/
theorem tree_gluingVerdict :
    tree.gluingVerdict (tree.chordList edgeListing.elems) boolListing.elems
        (fun edge chord => tree.mem_chordList (fun edge => edgeListing.complete ⟨_, _, edge⟩)
          edge chord)
        boolListing.complete =
      .refuted ⟨.c, .a, CycleEdge.ca, false,
        fun fixed => absurd (show (true : Bool) = false from fixed) (by decide)⟩ :=
  rfl

/-- **The spanning tree built in rounds** from the listed edges hangs `b` from `a` along `ab` and
`c` from `a` back along `ca`; its one chord is `bc`. -/
theorem roundsTree_chordList :
    (SpanningTree.ofEdges edgeListing reach).chordList edgeListing.elems =
      [⟨.b, .c, CycleEdge.bc⟩] :=
  rfl

/-- **The decision procedure for finite systems refutes gluing on the twisted cycle**, by the
correctness theorem. -/
theorem finiteGluingVerdict_refutes :
    (finiteGluingVerdict edgeListing boolListing reach).asBool = some false :=
  (finiteGluingVerdict_asBool_eq_false_iff _ _ _).mpr ⟨disparity⟩

/-- **The decision procedure for finite systems, run**: it finds the disparity at the one
fundamental cycle of the tree it builds, where the chord `bc` moves `false`. -/
theorem finiteGluingVerdict_eq :
    finiteGluingVerdict edgeListing boolListing reach =
      .refuted ⟨.b, .c, CycleEdge.bc, false,
        fun fixed => absurd (show (true : Bool) = false from fixed) (by decide)⟩ :=
  rfl

/-- A parent assignment around the cycle: every index, the root included, hangs from its
predecessor. -/
def cyclicParent : ∀ j : Vertex, Σ p : Vertex, twisted.Step p j
  | .a => ⟨.c, .forward CycleEdge.ca⟩
  | .b => ⟨.a, .forward CycleEdge.ab⟩
  | .c => ⟨.b, .forward CycleEdge.bc⟩

/-- Every edge of the twisted cycle is the link of the cyclic assignment at its target. -/
theorem cyclicParent_edge {i j : Vertex} (edge : twisted.Edge i j) :
    cyclicParent j = ⟨i, .forward edge⟩ := by
  change CycleEdge i j at edge
  cases edge <;> rfl

/-- **A spanning tree must be rooted**: the cyclic assignment makes every edge a parent link, so
no chord would remain to check, yet the twisted cycle has a disparity; no spanning tree uses the
assignment, since the root of a spanning tree has no parent. -/
theorem cyclic_parents_not_tree :
    (∀ {i j : Vertex} (edge : twisted.Edge i j), cyclicParent j = ⟨i, .forward edge⟩) ∧
      Nonempty (twisted.DisparityAt Vertex.a) ∧
      ∀ T : twisted.SpanningTree Vertex.a, T.parent Vertex.a ≠ some (cyclicParent Vertex.a) :=
  ⟨cyclicParent_edge, ⟨disparity.2⟩,
    fun T linked => nomatch T.parent_root.symm.trans linked⟩

instance pathEdgeDecidableEq (i j : Vertex) : DecidableEq (path.Edge i j) :=
  fun first second => isTrue (by
    change PathEdge i j at first second
    cases first <;> cases second <;> rfl)

instance pathViewDecidableEq (j : Vertex) : DecidableEq (path.View j) :=
  inferInstanceAs (DecidableEq Bool)

/-- The spanning tree of the untwisted path at `a`: the path itself. -/
def pathTree : path.SpanningTree Vertex.a where
  parent
    | .a => none
    | .b => some ⟨.a, .forward PathEdge.ab⟩
    | .c => some ⟨.b, .forward PathEdge.bc⟩
  path
    | .a => .nil _
    | .b => .forward PathEdge.ab (.nil _)
    | .c => .forward PathEdge.ab (.forward PathEdge.bc (.nil _))
  path_root := rfl
  eq_root
    | .a, _ => rfl
    | .b, missing => nomatch missing
    | .c, missing => nomatch missing
  path_parent
    | .a, _, _, linked => nomatch linked
    | .b, _, _, linked => by cases linked; rfl
    | .c, _, _, linked => by cases linked; rfl

/-- The two edges of the untwisted path. -/
def pathEdgeListing : Listing (Σ i j : Vertex, path.Edge i j) where
  elems := [⟨.a, .b, PathEdge.ab⟩, ⟨.b, .c, PathEdge.bc⟩]
  complete := fun ⟨i, j, edge⟩ => by
    change PathEdge i j at edge
    cases edge
    · exact List.Mem.head _
    · exact List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _)

/-- **No chord on the path**: there is no fundamental cycle to check. -/
theorem pathTree_chordList : pathTree.chordList pathEdgeListing.elems = [] :=
  rfl

/-- **The decision procedure establishes gluing on the path.** -/
theorem pathTree_gluingVerdict :
    (pathTree.gluingVerdict (pathTree.chordList pathEdgeListing.elems) boolListing.elems
        (fun edge chord => pathTree.mem_chordList
          (fun edge => pathEdgeListing.complete ⟨_, _, edge⟩) edge chord)
        boolListing.complete).asBool = some true :=
  rfl

end Twisted

namespace Swap

open ViewSystem DisparitySearch
open Twisted (Vertex CycleEdge)

instance swappedEdgeDecidableEq (i j : Vertex) : DecidableEq (swapped.Edge i j) :=
  fun first second => isTrue (by
    change CycleEdge i j at first second
    cases first <;> cases second <;> rfl)

instance swappedViewDecidableEq (j : Vertex) : DecidableEq (swapped.View j) :=
  inferInstanceAs (DecidableEq (Fin 3))

/-- The spanning tree of the swapped cycle at `a`, with `ca` as its only chord. -/
def tree : swapped.SpanningTree Vertex.a where
  parent
    | .a => none
    | .b => some ⟨.a, .forward CycleEdge.ab⟩
    | .c => some ⟨.b, .forward CycleEdge.bc⟩
  path
    | .a => .nil _
    | .b => .forward CycleEdge.ab (.nil _)
    | .c => .forward CycleEdge.ab (.forward CycleEdge.bc (.nil _))
  path_root := rfl
  eq_root
    | .a, _ => rfl
    | .b, missing => nomatch missing
    | .c, missing => nomatch missing
  path_parent
    | .a, _, _, linked => nomatch linked
    | .b, _, _, linked => by cases linked; rfl
    | .c, _, _, linked => by cases linked; rfl

/-- The three edges of the swapped cycle. -/
def edgeListing : Listing (Σ i j : Vertex, swapped.Edge i j) where
  elems := [⟨.a, .b, CycleEdge.ab⟩, ⟨.b, .c, CycleEdge.bc⟩, ⟨.c, .a, CycleEdge.ca⟩]
  complete := fun ⟨i, j, edge⟩ => by
    change CycleEdge i j at edge
    cases edge
    · exact List.Mem.head _
    · exact List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _)
    · exact List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _))

/-- The three points. -/
def pointListing : Listing (Fin 3) where
  elems := [0, 1, 2]
  complete
    | ⟨0, _⟩ => List.Mem.head _
    | ⟨1, _⟩ => List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _)
    | ⟨2, _⟩ => List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.tail _ (List.Mem.head _))
    | ⟨_ + 3, bound⟩ => absurd bound (by omega)

/-- **The search skips the fixed point and finds the swapped one**: the fundamental cycle of the
chord `ca` fixes `0` and moves `1`. -/
theorem tree_search :
    tree.search (tree.chordList edgeListing.elems) pointListing.elems =
      some ⟨.c, .a, CycleEdge.ca, (1 : Fin 3),
        fun fixed => absurd (show swapOneTwo 1 = 1 from fixed) (by decide)⟩ :=
  rfl

/-- Every closed walk at `a` fixes the point `0`. -/
theorem transport_fixes_zero (loop : swapped.Walk Vertex.a Vertex.a)
    (value : swapped.View Vertex.a) (zero : @Eq (Fin 3) value 0) :
    swapped.transport loop value = value := by
  subst zero
  rcases transport_cases loop with same | flipped
  · exact same _
  · exact flipped _

/-- The disparity of the swapped cycle at `1`, witnessed by distinctness. -/
def confirmable : swapped.ApartDisparity Vertex.a (SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq (Fin 3)) :=
  ⟨swappedCycle, (1 : Fin 3),
    fun fixed => absurd (show swapOneTwo 1 = 1 from fixed) (by decide)⟩

/-- **Walks first, values never, misses the disparity**: examining every closed walk with only the
fixed point `0` never reports, though the swapped cycle has a disparity at `1`. -/
theorem firstValueOnly_misses (loops : ℕ → Option (swapped.Walk Vertex.a Vertex.a))
    (values : ℕ → Option (Fin 3)) (first : values 0 = some 0) (stage : ℕ) :
    examine (S := swapped) (root := Vertex.a) (SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq (Fin 3))
      (firstValueOnly loops values) stage = none := by
  cases reported : examine (S := swapped) (root := Vertex.a) (SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq (Fin 3))
      (firstValueOnly loops values) stage with
  | none => rfl
  | some found =>
    exfalso
    obtain ⟨_, scheduled, _⟩ := examine_sound reported
    have moved : swapped.transport found.loop found.value ≠ found.value := found.apart
    exact moved (transport_fixes_zero found.loop found.value
      (Option.some.inj ((firstValueOnly_second scheduled).symm.trans first)))

/-- **Walks first, values never, is not fair**: the pair of the cycle and `1` is never
examined. -/
theorem firstValueOnly_not_fair (loops : ℕ → Option (swapped.Walk Vertex.a Vertex.a))
    (values : ℕ → Option (Fin 3)) (first : values 0 = some 0) :
    ¬ Fair (firstValueOnly loops values) := by
  intro fair
  obtain ⟨_, _, _, scheduled⟩ := fair (swappedCycle, (1 : Fin 3)) 0
  exact absurd (Option.some.inj ((firstValueOnly_second scheduled).symm.trans first)) (by decide)

/-- **The dovetailed search finds the disparity** whenever the cycle and the point `1` are
listed. -/
theorem dovetail_finds (loops : ℕ → Option (swapped.Walk Vertex.a Vertex.a))
    (values : ℕ → Option (Fin 3)) (listedLoop : ∃ r, loops r = some swappedCycle)
    (listedValue : ∃ s, values s = some 1) :
    ∃ stage, examine (SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq (Fin 3)) (dovetail loops values) stage =
      some confirmable :=
  examine_dovetail confirmable listedLoop listedValue

/-- The three points, enumerated. -/
def pointOfRank (rank : ℕ) : Option (Fin 3) :=
  if bound : rank < 3 then some ⟨rank, bound⟩ else none

theorem exists_pointOfRank_eq (point : Fin 3) : ∃ rank, pointOfRank rank = some point :=
  ⟨point.1, by
    unfold pointOfRank
    rw [dif_pos point.2]⟩

/-- **The fair search over every closed walk and every point reports every disparity of the
swapped cycle** at some finite stage; the closed walks are enumerated from the listed edges. -/
theorem closedWalks_search_complete (disparity : swapped.DisparityAt Vertex.a) :
    ∃ stage, examine (SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq (Fin 3))
        (dovetail (closedWalkOfRank (outStepsOfEdges edgeListing.elems) Vertex.a) pointOfRank)
        stage =
      some (ApartDisparity.ofDisparityAt (fun different => different) disparity) :=
  examine_complete_of_tight
    (dovetail_closedWalks_fair
      (mem_outStepsOfEdges fun edge => edgeListing.complete ⟨_, _, edge⟩) exists_pointOfRank_eq)
    _ disparity

/-- The fair search reports the disparity of the swapped cycle. -/
theorem closedWalks_search_reports :
    ∃ stage, (examine (SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq (Fin 3))
      (dovetail (closedWalkOfRank (outStepsOfEdges edgeListing.elems) Vertex.a) pointOfRank)
      stage).isSome = true := by
  obtain ⟨stage, reported⟩ := closedWalks_search_complete disparity.2
  exact ⟨stage, by rw [reported]; rfl⟩

/-- The edges of the swapped cycle, enumerated. -/
def edgeOfRank (rank : ℕ) : Option (Σ i j : Vertex, swapped.Edge i j) :=
  edgeListing.elems[rank]?

theorem exists_edgeOfRank_eq {i j : Vertex} (edge : swapped.Edge i j) :
    ∃ rank, edgeOfRank rank = some ⟨i, j, edge⟩ :=
  List.mem_iff_getElem?.mp (edgeListing.complete _)

/-- **The fair search over the three fundamental cycles and every point reports a disparity of
the swapped cycle**, by the reduction to fundamental cycles. -/
theorem cycles_search_reports :
    ∃ stage, (examine (SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq (Fin 3))
      (dovetail (tree.cycleOfRank edgeOfRank) pointOfRank) stage).isSome = true :=
  tree.exists_examine_cycles (SemiApartness.ofDecidableEq_cotransitive (Fin 3))
    exists_edgeOfRank_eq exists_pointOfRank_eq confirmable

end Swap

namespace Apart

open ViewSystem

/-- No walk reaches `false` from `true`. -/
theorem walk_true_false_empty : IsEmpty (apart.Walk true false) :=
  ⟨fun walk => by
    cases walk with
    | forward edge _ => exact Empty.elim edge
    | backward edge _ => exact Empty.elim edge⟩

/-- **No spanning tree**: the index graph is not connected. -/
theorem no_spanningTree : IsEmpty (apart.SpanningTree true) :=
  ⟨fun tree => walk_true_false_empty.false (tree.path false)⟩

/-- **A spanning tree is needed**: holonomy at `true` is trivial, so no closed walk there moves a
value, yet the views do not glue; no spanning tree exists. -/
theorem trivial_at_root_without_tree :
    apart.TrivialHolonomyAt true ∧ IsEmpty (apart.SpanningTree true) ∧
      ¬ Nonempty apart.Gluing :=
  ⟨fun loop value => apart_trivialHolonomy loop value, no_spanningTree, no_gluing⟩

end Apart

namespace FlipStream

open ViewSystem DisparitySearch

/-- Flip one position of a boolean stream, an involution. -/
def flipAt (k : ℕ) : (ℕ → Bool) ≃ (ℕ → Bool) where
  toFun stream n := xor (stream n) (n == k)
  invFun stream n := xor (stream n) (n == k)
  left_inv stream := funext fun n => by
    show xor (xor (stream n) (n == k)) (n == k) = stream n
    cases stream n <;> cases n == k <;> rfl
  right_inv stream := funext fun n => by
    show xor (xor (stream n) (n == k)) (n == k) = stream n
    cases stream n <;> cases n == k <;> rfl

/-- **One index with one loop**: the views are boolean streams and the loop flips position `1`.
Equality of the views is not decidable. -/
def flipLoop : ViewSystem.{0, 0, 0} Unit where
  View _ := ℕ → Bool
  Edge _ _ := Unit
  translate _ := flipAt 1

/-- Once around the loop. -/
def turn : flipLoop.Walk () () :=
  .forward () (.nil ())

/-- The stream that is false everywhere. -/
def zeroStream : ℕ → Bool :=
  fun _ => false

/-- **The loop moves the zero stream apart**: the two differ at position `1`. -/
def turnDisparity : flipLoop.ApartDisparity () SemiApartness.streams :=
  ⟨turn, zeroStream, ⟨1, by decide⟩⟩

/-- Every walk keeps position `0`. -/
theorem transport_keeps_zero : ∀ {i j : Unit} (walk : flipLoop.Walk i j) (stream : ℕ → Bool),
    flipLoop.transport walk stream 0 = stream 0
  | _, _, .nil _, _ => rfl
  | _, _, .forward _ rest, stream => (transport_keeps_zero rest _).trans (by
      show xor (stream 0) (0 == 1) = stream 0
      cases stream 0 <;> rfl)
  | _, _, .backward _ rest, stream => (transport_keeps_zero rest _).trans (by
      show xor (stream 0) (0 == 1) = stream 0
      cases stream 0 <;> rfl)

/-- At budget `0` the test compares position `0` only. -/
theorem streams_test_zero {first second : ℕ → Bool} (same : first 0 = second 0) :
    SemiApartness.streams.test first second 0 = false := by
  show ((first 0 != second 0) || false) = false
  rw [same, bne_self_eq_false]
  rfl

/-- **Budgets matter**: the test does not confirm the disparity at budget `0` and confirms it at
budget `1`. -/
theorem turn_test : SemiApartness.streams.test (flipLoop.transport turn zeroStream) zeroStream 0 =
      false ∧
    SemiApartness.streams.test (flipLoop.transport turn zeroStream) zeroStream 1 = true :=
  ⟨rfl, rfl⟩

/-- **A fixed budget misses the disparity**: at budget `0` the test compares position `0` only,
which no closed walk changes. -/
theorem zeroBudget_misses (loops : ℕ → Option (flipLoop.Walk () ()))
    (values : ℕ → Option (ℕ → Bool)) (stage : ℕ) :
    examine (S := flipLoop) (root := ()) SemiApartness.streams (zeroBudget loops values) stage =
      none := by
  cases reported : examine (S := flipLoop) (root := ()) SemiApartness.streams
      (zeroBudget loops values) stage with
  | none => rfl
  | some found =>
    exfalso
    obtain ⟨budget, scheduled, confirmed⟩ := examine_sound reported
    have budgetZero : budget = 0 := zeroBudget_budget scheduled
    subst budgetZero
    exact nomatch (streams_test_zero (transport_keeps_zero found.loop found.value)).symm.trans
      confirmed

/-- **A fixed budget is not fair**: no pair is ever examined at budget `1`. -/
theorem zeroBudget_not_fair (loops : ℕ → Option (flipLoop.Walk () ()))
    (values : ℕ → Option (ℕ → Bool)) : ¬ Fair (zeroBudget loops values) := by
  intro fair
  obtain ⟨_, _, enough, scheduled⟩ := fair (turn, zeroStream) 1
  rw [zeroBudget_budget scheduled] at enough
  exact absurd enough (by decide)

/-- **The dovetailed search finds the disparity** whenever the loop and the zero stream are
listed. -/
theorem dovetail_finds (loops : ℕ → Option (flipLoop.Walk () ()))
    (values : ℕ → Option (ℕ → Bool)) (listedLoop : ∃ r, loops r = some turn)
    (listedValue : ∃ s, values s = some zeroStream) :
    ∃ stage, examine SemiApartness.streams (dovetail loops values) stage = some turnDisparity :=
  examine_dovetail turnDisparity listedLoop listedValue

/-- **The budgeted verdict**: listing the loop and the zero stream at every rank, the first two
stages examine budget `0` and leave the verdict incomplete; the third examines budget `1` and
refutes gluing. -/
theorem searchVerdict_stages :
    searchVerdict SemiApartness.streams
        (dovetail (fun _ => some turn) (fun _ => some zeroStream)) 2 = .incomplete 2 ∧
      (searchVerdict SemiApartness.streams
        (dovetail (fun _ => some turn) (fun _ => some zeroStream)) 3).asBool = some false :=
  ⟨rfl, rfl⟩

/-- The spanning tree of the loop: one index without a parent, so the loop is the only chord. -/
def loopTree : flipLoop.SpanningTree () where
  parent _ := none
  path
    | () => .nil ()
  path_root := rfl
  eq_root
    | (), _ => rfl
  path_parent _ _ _ linked := nomatch linked

/-- Three times around the loop. -/
def thrice : flipLoop.Walk () () :=
  .forward (j := ()) () (.forward (j := ()) () (.forward (j := ()) () (.nil ())))

/-- **The reduction to fundamental cycles needs no decidable equality**: three turns move the
zero stream apart, so some fundamental cycle moves some stream apart. -/
theorem thrice_reduces :
    ∃ (source target : Unit) (edge : flipLoop.Edge source target) (point : ℕ → Bool),
      SemiApartness.streams.Apart (flipLoop.transport (loopTree.cycle edge) point) point :=
  loopTree.exists_cycle_apart SemiApartness.streams_cotransitive
    ⟨thrice, zeroStream, ⟨1, by decide⟩⟩

end FlipStream

end Mettapedia.GSLT.Scope

